@startuml
title Finance Management Platform - GUI Component Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Personal User" as PersonalUser
actor "Household Member" as HouseholdUser <<planned>>
actor "Company Finance User" as BusinessUser <<planned>>

package "GUI Layer" {
  [gui.py\nFinanceApp\nPackaged GUI] as GUI
  [FinanceDashboard] as Dashboard
}

package "Core Business Layer" {
  [Shared Application State\nFinanceApplicationState] as AppState
  [Transaction Service\nTransactionManager] as Transactions
  [Budget Service\nBudgetManager] as Budgets
  [Dashboard Analytics\nbuild_dashboard_data] as Analytics
}

package "Persistence Layer" {
  [Storage Facade\nStorageManager] as Storage
  [SQLite Storage\nSQLiteStorage] as SQLiteStorage
  [Custom Data Structures] as Structures
}

package "Domain Models" {
  [Transaction] as Transaction
  [Category] as Category
  [Budget] as Budget
  [DashboardData] as DashboardData
}

database "Shared data/finance_tracker.db\n(SQLite)" as Ledger

PersonalUser --> GUI : Desktop GUI
HouseholdUser ..> GUI : Future household GUI <<planned>>
BusinessUser ..> GUI : Future company-finance GUI <<planned>>

GUI --> AppState : Load and save shared state
GUI --> Dashboard : Lazy creation

AppState --> Transactions
AppState --> Budgets
AppState --> Storage

Dashboard --> Analytics
Analytics --> DashboardData
Analytics --> Transaction

Transactions --> Transaction
Transactions --> Category
Transactions --> Structures
Budgets --> Budget

Storage --> SQLiteStorage
SQLiteStorage --> Ledger : Atomic transactions and revision checks

note bottom of GUI
  This is the primary interface for end users.
  Household and company-finance GUI capabilities are planned.
end note

note bottom of AppState
  Transactions and budgets are serialized as one complete state
  and committed to the shared SQLite database together.
end note

@enduml
